H("884.d.1.A",4,"Inez finds fraying insulation on the cord of a drill in the fleet garage. The safest move is to:","tag the drill out of service until the cord is repaired",["wrap the cord in tape and keep drilling","hand it to a coworker","use it only outdoors"],"Remove damaged tools.")
H("884.d.1.B",3,"A fleet shop's manager walks the garage each month with a checklist to find hazards and fix them. This describes:","using audits and inspections to maintain compliance with safety, health and environmental regulations",["avoiding rules","skipping logs","hiding hazards"],"Audits.")
H("884.d.1.B",4,"An inspection log in a transportation shop is valuable because it:","documents when problems were found and fixed",["hides problems","replaces training","adds hazards"],"Records show compliance.")
H("884.d.2.A",3,"On a delivery van, a student labels the engine, the brakes, the suspension and the electrical system. She is:","identifying the major components in a vehicular system",["naming only the paint","naming only the seats","naming only the tires"],"Name the systems.")
H("884.d.2.A",4,"Which of these is a part of a vehicle's braking system?","Master cylinder",["Alternator","Radiator","Spark plug"],"Brake part.")
H("884.d.2.B",3,"A fleet mechanic schedules a coolant flush and a belt replacement based on the miles on a bus. He is:","identifying necessary maintenance and service of vehicular systems",["ignoring service","guessing","waiting for failure"],"Scheduled service.")
H("884.d.2.B",4,"Following the manufacturer's service interval for oil changes helps:","protect the engine from wear",["wear out the engine","raise fuel waste","hide leaks"],"Interval service.")
H("884.d.2.C",3,"A fleet adopts a plan that checks tires, fluids and lights on every truck weekly so breakdowns stay low. This is:","a preventative maintenance plan to keep vehicular systems in good working order",["waiting for failure","random repairs","no plan"],"Preventive plan.")
H("884.d.2.C",4,"Compared with waiting for a breakdown, preventative maintenance usually:","lowers downtime and repair cost over time",["raises downtime","adds breakdowns","ignores problems"],"Prevent costly failures.")
H("884.d.3.A",3,"A student studies how trucking, rail and shipping move food, fuel and goods that people in a city depend on. She is identifying:","the scope and effect on society of the energy and power of transportation systems",["no effect","only paint colors","only hobby cars"],"Society depends on transportation.")
